The system's name, as people see it.

Visible names are ours: PRETTY_NAME and NAME in os-release,
DISTRIB_DESCRIPTION in lsb-release, the login prompt (issue) and the
welcome text (legal).

Identifiers that programs read to decide compatibility are left as Ubuntu's:
ID=ubuntu, DISTRIB_ID=Ubuntu and the release codename. Third-party
installers, extra package repositories and driver tools check these.

The files belong to Ubuntu's base-files package; build-iso.sh diverts them
so that package updates do not put Ubuntu's versions back.
